MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Blue & Lonesome and Step Back feel like natural next choices because their blues focus connects with what draws me to Old Sock, Memphis, and People, Hell & Angels.",
    "Old Yellow Moon and Ryan Adams also make sense because their songwriting could connect with my interest in You Should Be So Lucky, even though blues is my stronger preference today."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The Endless River's atmospheric instrumental direction misses the blues and song-driven listening I want right now, despite its connection to rock.",
    "I cannot tell whether Soul City fits from the title alone, so I would skip it rather than spend one of my few interactions exploring an uncertain match."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My interest in some rock albums seems to have been stretched into an interest in atmospheric rock, where the musical experience feels quite different.",
    "Familiar rock songs are only part of the appeal for me; Grrr: Greatest Hits is less compelling today because I want to explore a studio album."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "The guitar-led blues connection across several recent choices matters more to me today than a broad connection to rock.",
    "An album can fit my taste without prompting me to act: I would choose Blue & Lonesome and Step Back, then stop, even though several other suggestions appeal."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations mostly recognize my blues and roots interests, but some stretch my rock interest beyond the guitar-led, song-driven music I want today."
}
